cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use gmlst, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "gmlst: unified MLST, cgMLST and scheme-free bacterial typing from assemblies and reads with swappable alignment backends"
authors:
  - family-names: Yu
    given-names: Hua
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6896-8056"
    affiliation: "Hangzhou Center for Disease Control and Prevention, Hangzhou, China"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23072500
version: 0.5.4
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/indexofire/gmlst"
abstract: >-
  gmlst unifies classical MLST, cgMLST/wgMLST and scheme-free typing in
  one command-line interface for assemblies and raw reads, with swappable
  BLAST+, KMA, minimap2 and MUMmer4 backends, unified access to PubMLST,
  Pasteur BIGSdb, EnteroBase and cgmlst.org schemes with API-key
  authentication, a two-layer exact-hash and k-mer pre-resolution,
  novel-allele extraction into local laboratory schemes, built-in minimum
  spanning trees, and an automation-first interface suited to scripts,
  workflow engines and autonomous agents.
keywords:
  - bacterial typing
  - MLST
  - cgMLST
  - epidemiology
  - genomics
